{"id":"e48ecbf40a3c92b6","group":"73","path":"73/73-thm-finite-automaton-pumping.md","title":"Pumping Lemma for Regular Languages","display":"thm-regular-pumping-lemma — Pumping Lemma for Regular Languages","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Introduction to Automata Theory, Languages, and Computation (Hopcroft, Motwani, Ullman; 3rd ed., 2007)","book_abbrev":"73","label":"73-thm-finite-automaton-pumping","aliases":["73-thm-finite-automaton-pumping","73-thm-regular-pumping-lemma"],"display":"thm-regular-pumping-lemma — Pumping Lemma for Regular Languages","depends_on":["[[73-df-finite-automaton-language-class]]","[[73-df-language-pumping-length]]"],"source_id":"HMU2007","source_ref":"§4.1, print pp. 128–133; PDF pp. 150–155","source_status":"third-edition-topic-mapped; inherited-local-review; not-a-line-by-line-source-proof-certificate","reviewed_on":"2026-10-24","legacy_source_id":"HU1979","legacy_source_ref":"§3.1, pp. 55–58; local typed pumping statement","legacy_source_status":"local-formalization; source-section-located; proof scope recorded in review","revision_round":"pdf-third-edition-20261024","edition_role":"third-edition-core","third_edition_chapter":4},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Introduction to Automata Theory, Languages, and Computation (Hopcroft, Motwani, Ullman; 3rd ed., 2007)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"73"},{"key":"label","html":"73-thm-finite-automaton-pumping"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>73-thm-finite-automaton-pumping</span><span>73-thm-regular-pumping-lemma</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-regular-pumping-lemma — Pumping Lemma for Regular Languages"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"c284ffb568a496fd\" href=\"?note=c284ffb568a496fd\" title=\"73-df-finite-automaton-language-class\">73-df-finite-automaton-language-class</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"01b7b9d9615ddaa5\" href=\"?note=01b7b9d9615ddaa5\" title=\"73-df-language-pumping-length\">73-df-language-pumping-length</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_id","html":"HMU2007"},{"key":"source_ref","html":"§4.1, print pp. 128–133; PDF pp. 150–155"},{"key":"source_status","html":"third-edition-topic-mapped; inherited-local-review; not-a-line-by-line-source-proof-certificate"},{"key":"reviewed_on","html":"2026-10-24"},{"key":"legacy_source_id","html":"HU1979"},{"key":"legacy_source_ref","html":"§3.1, pp. 55–58; local typed pumping statement"},{"key":"legacy_source_status","html":"local-formalization; source-section-located; proof scope recorded in review"},{"key":"revision_round","html":"pdf-third-edition-20261024"},{"key":"edition_role","html":"third-edition-core"},{"key":"third_edition_chapter","html":"4"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span> (alphabet)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\\in\\mathsf{REG}_{\\Sigma}\">\\(L\\in\\mathsf{REG}_{\\Sigma}\\)</span> (regular language, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"c284ffb568a496fd\" href=\"?note=c284ffb568a496fd\" title=\"73-df-finite-automaton-language-class\">73-df-finite-automaton-language-class</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)\">\\(p_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)\\)</span> (canonical pumping length, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"01b7b9d9615ddaa5\" href=\"?note=01b7b9d9615ddaa5\" title=\"73-df-language-pumping-length\">73-df-language-pumping-length</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}regular\\text{-}pumping\\text{-}lemma}\\vdash\n\\forall w\\in L\\;\n\\Bigl(\n|w|\\geq p_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)\\to\n\\exists x,y,z\\in\\Sigma^*\\;\n\\bigl(\nw=xyz\\land |xy|\\leq p_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)\\land |y|\\geq1\n\\land\\forall i\\in\\mathbb N\\;(xy^iz\\in L)\n\\bigr)\n\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}regular\\text{-}pumping\\text{-}lemma}\\vdash\n\\forall w\\in L\\;\n\\Bigl(\n|w|\\geq p_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)\\to\n\\exists x,y,z\\in\\Sigma^*\\;\n\\bigl(\nw=xyz\\land |xy|\\leq p_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)\\land |y|\\geq1\n\\land\\forall i\\in\\mathbb N\\;(xy^iz\\in L)\n\\bigr)\n\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Among the first <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)+1\">\\(p_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)+1\\)</span> states of the accepting run, two coincide. The intervening nonempty segment is <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"y\">\\(y\\)</span>, and repeating or deleting its loop preserves the final state.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"73-df-finite-automaton-language-class","status":"resolved","id":"c284ffb568a496fd","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-finite-automaton-language-class]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-language-pumping-length","status":"resolved","id":"01b7b9d9615ddaa5","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-language-pumping-length]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-finite-automaton-language-class","status":"resolved","id":"c284ffb568a496fd","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$L\\in\\mathsf{REG}_{\\Sigma}$ (regular language, see [[73-df-finite-automaton-language-class]])","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-language-pumping-length","status":"resolved","id":"01b7b9d9615ddaa5","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$p_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)$ (canonical pumping length, see [[73-df-language-pumping-length]])","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"\\Sigma","display":false},{"tex":"L\\in\\mathsf{REG}_{\\Sigma}","display":false},{"tex":"p_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}regular\\text{-}pumping\\text{-}lemma}\\vdash\n\\forall w\\in L\\;\n\\Bigl(\n|w|\\geq p_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)\\to\n\\exists x,y,z\\in\\Sigma^*\\;\n\\bigl(\nw=xyz\\land |xy|\\leq p_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)\\land |y|\\geq1\n\\land\\forall i\\in\\mathbb N\\;(xy^iz\\in L)\n\\bigr)\n\\Bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"p_{\\mathsf{reg}}(L)+1","display":false},{"tex":"y","display":false}],"bytes":1717,"backlinks":[{"id":"95218b81d22ed54f","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"432c4bc700976332","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"6af52783a9bce985","anchor":"ref-65","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[73-thm-finite-automaton-pumping|Pumping Lemma for Regular Languages]]"},{"id":"f5ad19f3a79bf5de","anchor":"ref-6","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$M=(Q,\\Sigma,\\delta,q_0,F)$、$N=(P,\\Sigma,\\eta,p_0,H)$ 为同一字母表上的 DFA；令 $n=|Q|,m=|P|$。语言语义、泵引理和乘积见 [[73-df-dfa-language-semantics]]、[[73-thm-finite-automaton-pumping]]、[[73-df-dfa-product]]、[[73-thm-dfa-product-correctness]]。"},{"id":"1dd8b3118783dcb5","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""}],"outgoing":["c284ffb568a496fd","01b7b9d9615ddaa5"]}